# Reduction of USC Mech II: methodology, validation and accuracy/complexity trade-off

**Run:** autonomous kinetic mechanism reduction, 2026-09-16 (single day, resource-limited).
**Parent mechanism:** USC Mech II (Wang et al., 2007), 111 species / 784 reactions,
H2/CO/C1–C4 hydrocarbon oxidation, supplied as `mechs/parent.yaml` (Cantera YAML
converted from the USC CTI file). All reduced mechanisms below are derived from
this file by *removing whole species and reactions only* — no rate, thermo or
transport parameter was refitted. Elemental conservation is therefore inherited
exactly (every reaction verified element-balanced at build time), and the
parent's NASA-polynomial fits (including its few documented mid-T discontinuities)
are preserved verbatim. Toolchain: Cantera 3.2.0 + custom Python workflow (`src/`),
local 2-core workstation + 64-core remote batch nodes.

